WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
First Revenue Game helps a solo builder turn one monetizable skill into first-revenue evidence—not generic task activity.

00:12.000 --> 00:24.000
The workspace keeps one active commercial mission, its proof standard, due date, fallback, and revenue goal together.

00:24.000 --> 00:36.000
Submitted proof enters a server-confirmed review state and locks editing so the decision remains tied to the exact evidence.

00:36.000 --> 00:48.000
The operator can reject with an actionable note or approve only the milestones the submitted proof supports.

00:48.000 --> 01:00.000
The same mission-first hierarchy remains usable on mobile, with access to pod accountability, progress, and settings.

01:00.000 --> 01:15.000
Next.js is the shell; Spring Boot owns the configured workflow, with PostgreSQL, a transactional outbox, Redpanda, and observable event evidence.
